    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-zoho-agreements-2b-s3-20260724",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 2524,
      "width": 820,
      "height": 90,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (2B-S3): zoho_agreements joins adobe_agreements as the e-signature\nreverse index (requestId/agreementId -> the ERP proposta + owning app/user). Tiny + NON-\nsensitive (no credentials); the inbound webhook never trusts the row for signature state. Both\nstores ride the ch10 import passthrough (import-tool.ts) so a prod cutover carries them verbatim.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (2B-S3): zoho_agreements joins adobe_agreements as the e-signature\nreverse index (requestId/agreementId -> the ERP proposta + owning app/user). Tiny + NON-\nsensitive (no credentials); the inbound webhook never trusts the row for signature state. Both\nstores ride the ch10 import passthrough (import-tool.ts) so a prod cutover carries them verbatim.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 42119001,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 42119777,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (2B-S3): zoho_agreements joins adobe_agreements as the e-signature\nreverse index (requestId/agreementId -> the ERP proposta + owning app/user). Tiny + NON-\nsensitive (no credentials); the inbound webhook never trusts the row for signature state. Both\nstores ride the ch10 import passthrough (import-tool.ts) so a prod cutover carries them verbatim."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-2a1",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 840,
      "height": 105,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Listener rail, 2A-S1): NEW listener_state collection (_id = triggerId) holds\neach kind:'listener' trigger's durable poll cursor / high-water mark + a failure counter. The\nsupervisor advances the cursor ONLY after every polled item is durably enqueued into event_queue\n(cursor-advance-only-after-enqueue): a crash re-polls the boundary rather than dropping events.\ntriggers rows gain optional kind ('webhook'|'listener', absent=>webhook) + pollConfig - additive,\nmigration-free (existing rows keep working).",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Listener rail, 2A-S1): NEW listener_state collection (_id = triggerId) holds\neach kind:'listener' trigger's durable poll cursor / high-water mark + a failure counter. The\nsupervisor advances the cursor ONLY after every polled item is durably enqueued into event_queue\n(cursor-advance-only-after-enqueue): a crash re-polls the boundary rather than dropping events.\ntriggers rows gain optional kind ('webhook'|'listener', absent=>webhook) + pollConfig - additive,\nmigration-free (existing rows keep working).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 1151320387,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 656764798,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Listener rail, 2A-S1): NEW listener_state collection (_id = triggerId) holds\neach kind:'listener' trigger's durable poll cursor / high-water mark + a failure counter. The\nsupervisor advances the cursor ONLY after every polled item is durably enqueued into event_queue\n(cursor-advance-only-after-enqueue): a crash re-polls the boundary rather than dropping events.\ntriggers rows gain optional kind ('webhook'|'listener', absent=>webhook) + pollConfig - additive,\nmigration-free (existing rows keep working)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-memvault-e2-0a6fea56",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 2895,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 157.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): a NEW per-USER filesystem plane beside the org-partitioned\nknowledge vault - <memvault root>/<userId>/<permalink>.md, one plain-markdown file per note with YAML\nfrontmatter a stock `basic-memory sync` can index (title, type, permalink, tags + created/modified;\nJSON-encoded scalars / flow-style tags array, the knowledge/vault.ts convention). Permalink grammar is\nthe isolation boundary: [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-_]* segments joined by '/', max 512 - no dots, so traversal is\nunrepresentable. No Mongo collection: state IS the files; the durable trace is one activity row per call\n(category 'memvault', metadata op/verdict/ms/permalink + keyId/xClient on key-admitted calls). Wire\nshapes: shared/src/memvault.ts (NoteRecord/WriteNoteRequest/NoteListResponse...). List pages are\nmetadata-only; the body travels only on readNote. E3 (search/export) reads this same format.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): a NEW per-USER filesystem plane beside the org-partitioned\nknowledge vault - <memvault root>/<userId>/<permalink>.md, one plain-markdown file per note with YAML\nfrontmatter a stock `basic-memory sync` can index (title, type, permalink, tags + created/modified;\nJSON-encoded scalars / flow-style tags array, the knowledge/vault.ts convention). Permalink grammar is\nthe isolation boundary: [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-_]* segments joined by '/', max 512 - no dots, so traversal is\nunrepresentable. No Mongo collection: state IS the files; the durable trace is one activity row per call\n(category 'memvault', metadata op/verdict/ms/permalink + keyId/xClient on key-admitted calls). Wire\nshapes: shared/src/memvault.ts (NoteRecord/WriteNoteRequest/NoteListResponse...). List pages are\nmetadata-only; the body travels only on readNote. E3 (search/export) reads this same format.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 1273790513,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1635286725,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): a NEW per-USER filesystem plane beside the org-partitioned\nknowledge vault - <memvault root>/<userId>/<permalink>.md, one plain-markdown file per note with YAML\nfrontmatter a stock `basic-memory sync` can index (title, type, permalink, tags + created/modified;\nJSON-encoded scalars / flow-style tags array, the knowledge/vault.ts convention). Permalink grammar is\nthe isolation boundary: [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-_]* segments joined by '/', max 512 - no dots, so traversal is\nunrepresentable. No Mongo collection: state IS the files; the durable trace is one activity row per call\n(category 'memvault', metadata op/verdict/ms/permalink + keyId/xClient on key-admitted calls). Wire\nshapes: shared/src/memvault.ts (NoteRecord/WriteNoteRequest/NoteListResponse...). List pages are\nmetadata-only; the body travels only on readNote. E3 (search/export) reads this same format."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-memvault-e3-5f28ab61",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 3080,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 367.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): the per-user filesystem plane gains ONE\nRESERVED, DERIVED artifact - <memvault root>/<userId>/.index/notes.db, a SQLite FTS5 database (columns\npermalink UNINDEXED, title, tags, body; tokenize unicode61 remove_diacritics 2, so 'acoes' finds 'ações').\nStill NO Mongo collection anywhere in memvault. TENANCY IS PHYSICAL AT THE FILE LEVEL: one database per user,\nnever a shared table with an owner column - a cross-tenant hit has no representation to leak through. The db\nfile AND its SQLite sidecars are containment-checked individually (a directory-only check let a planted\nnotes.db symlink cross tenants in both directions).\nTHE INDEX IS DERIVED AND IS NEVER TRUSTED OVER THE FILES. It is rebuilt from the user's own tree (and only\nthat tree) when it is missing, zero-byte, corrupt, EMPTY, or merely OUT OF STEP with the markdown - the last\none via a row-count reconcile on every cache miss, which needs no marker and so survives a restart even when\nthe file could not be deleted. Note the size trap behind the emptiness probe: a created-but-never-filled FTS5\ndatabase is 24,576 bytes, exactly the size of a populated one, so no file-size heuristic can tell them apart;\noutright damage takes the other path and throws (SQLITE_CORRUPT / SQLITE_NOTADB).\n'.index' is dot-prefixed on purpose: the permalink grammar has no '.', so it is unaddressable as a note,\ninvisible to the list walk, and absent from the export by construction.\nExport shape: GET /api/v1/memvault/export streams an uncompressed ustar of <permalink>.md entries carrying the\nfile's verbatim bytes (frontmatter + body), permalink-ascending, mode 0644, mtime = the note's own `modified` -\nso an unchanged vault exports byte-identically. Search shape: {hits:[{permalink,title,snippet?,score?}]}\n(BM25, title-weighted, larger-is-better). Permalink grammar tightened: each SEGMENT is capped at 200 chars\n(NOTE_PERMALINK_SEGMENT_MAX) beside the 512 total - one segment is one path component and the filesystem limit\nis 255 bytes, which a contract-valid 300-char permalink used to blow past with ENAMETOOLONG (E2 review F1).",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): the per-user filesystem plane gains ONE\nRESERVED, DERIVED artifact - <memvault root>/<userId>/.index/notes.db, a SQLite FTS5 database (columns\npermalink UNINDEXED, title, tags, body; tokenize unicode61 remove_diacritics 2, so 'acoes' finds 'ações').\nStill NO Mongo collection anywhere in memvault. TENANCY IS PHYSICAL AT THE FILE LEVEL: one database per user,\nnever a shared table with an owner column - a cross-tenant hit has no representation to leak through. The db\nfile AND its SQLite sidecars are containment-checked individually (a directory-only check let a planted\nnotes.db symlink cross tenants in both directions).\nTHE INDEX IS DERIVED AND IS NEVER TRUSTED OVER THE FILES. It is rebuilt from the user's own tree (and only\nthat tree) when it is missing, zero-byte, corrupt, EMPTY, or merely OUT OF STEP with the markdown - the last\none via a row-count reconcile on every cache miss, which needs no marker and so survives a restart even when\nthe file could not be deleted. Note the size trap behind the emptiness probe: a created-but-never-filled FTS5\ndatabase is 24,576 bytes, exactly the size of a populated one, so no file-size heuristic can tell them apart;\noutright damage takes the other path and throws (SQLITE_CORRUPT / SQLITE_NOTADB).\n'.index' is dot-prefixed on purpose: the permalink grammar has no '.', so it is unaddressable as a note,\ninvisible to the list walk, and absent from the export by construction.\nExport shape: GET /api/v1/memvault/export streams an uncompressed ustar of <permalink>.md entries carrying the\nfile's verbatim bytes (frontmatter + body), permalink-ascending, mode 0644, mtime = the note's own `modified` -\nso an unchanged vault exports byte-identically. Search shape: {hits:[{permalink,title,snippet?,score?}]}\n(BM25, title-weighted, larger-is-better). Permalink grammar tightened: each SEGMENT is capped at 200 chars\n(NOTE_PERMALINK_SEGMENT_MAX) beside the 512 total - one segment is one path component and the filesystem limit\nis 255 bytes, which a contract-valid 300-char permalink used to blow past with ENAMETOOLONG (E2 review F1).",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (memvault, slice E3 + its fresh-context review): the per-user filesystem plane gains ONE\nRESERVED, DERIVED artifact - <memvault root>/<userId>/.index/notes.db, a SQLite FTS5 database (columns\npermalink UNINDEXED, title, tags, body; tokenize unicode61 remove_diacritics 2, so 'acoes' finds 'ações').\nStill NO Mongo collection anywhere in memvault. TENANCY IS PHYSICAL AT THE FILE LEVEL: one database per user,\nnever a shared table with an owner column - a cross-tenant hit has no representation to leak through. The db\nfile AND its SQLite sidecars are containment-checked individually (a directory-only check let a planted\nnotes.db symlink cross tenants in both directions).\nTHE INDEX IS DERIVED AND IS NEVER TRUSTED OVER THE FILES. It is rebuilt from the user's own tree (and only\nthat tree) when it is missing, zero-byte, corrupt, EMPTY, or merely OUT OF STEP with the markdown - the last\none via a row-count reconcile on every cache miss, which needs no marker and so survives a restart even when\nthe file could not be deleted. Note the size trap behind the emptiness probe: a created-but-never-filled FTS5\ndatabase is 24,576 bytes, exactly the size of a populated one, so no file-size heuristic can tell them apart;\noutright damage takes the other path and throws (SQLITE_CORRUPT / SQLITE_NOTADB).\n'.index' is dot-prefixed on purpose: the permalink grammar has no '.', so it is unaddressable as a note,\ninvisible to the list walk, and absent from the export by construction.\nExport shape: GET /api/v1/memvault/export streams an uncompressed ustar of <permalink>.md entries carrying the\nfile's verbatim bytes (frontmatter + body), permalink-ascending, mode 0644, mtime = the note's own `modified` -\nso an unchanged vault exports byte-identically. Search shape: {hits:[{permalink,title,snippet?,score?}]}\n(BM25, title-weighted, larger-is-better). Permalink grammar tightened: each SEGMENT is capped at 200 chars\n(NOTE_PERMALINK_SEGMENT_MAX) beside the 512 total - one segment is one path component and the filesystem limit\nis 255 bytes, which a contract-valid 300-char permalink used to blow past with ENAMETOOLONG (E2 review F1).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 1962440813,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 742118903,
      "isDeleted": false,
