      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice B2) - THE INTEGRATION -> COFRE-ITEM JOIN (WS-C shadow).\nintegration_configs gains cofreItemId; cofre_items gains integrationLink {integrationKey, configId}. The join\nis two-way and BOTH halves are stamped server-side: the wire schema CofreItemCreateRequest does not declare\nintegrationLink, so a client cannot forge the provenance. Every read re-checks it - an item id alone is not\nauthority, so a config pointed at another integration's, another config's or another tenant's item is refused\nbefore anything decrypts, with the same uniform NOT_FOUND a missing id gets.\nCUSTODY: the item value is the WHOLE config-values bundle, JSON, encrypted through the same org-bound v2\nenvelope as credentialsCiphertext (data/crypto envelopeEncrypt) - one crypto path, not a second one to audit.\nItems stay OWNER-scoped (decisions.md 2026-07-27): an org-shared config's item belongs to the admin who typed\nit, so a same-org peer is 'unreachable' and keeps the pre-WS-C binding - the residual for the cutover review.\nRULE 10: credentialsCiphertext is still the LIVE read; the Cofre item is the SHADOW, and every credential read\nat the composition-root seam runs compareCredentialShadow (match | drift | shadow_absent | shadow_unreachable |\nshadow_locked | shadow_refused | legacy_absent | shadow_error). The report carries field NAMES only, never a\nvalue. CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE 2026-08-15 (decisions.md), matching the legacy-runtime-tier review date.\nNOT shadowed - live from day one: the credential-egress allow-list is now the ITEM's boundOrigins (empty, i.e.\nREFUSE, once the grant is revoked), not a derivation from the definition an agent authors. Reserved rows\n(platform-oauth / pipedream) are out of WS-C scope and mint nothing.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice B2) - THE INTEGRATION -> COFRE-ITEM JOIN (WS-C shadow).\nintegration_configs gains cofreItemId; cofre_items gains integrationLink {integrationKey, configId}. The join\nis two-way and BOTH halves are stamped server-side: the wire schema CofreItemCreateRequest does not declare\nintegrationLink, so a client cannot forge the provenance. Every read re-checks it - an item id alone is not\nauthority, so a config pointed at another integration's, another config's or another tenant's item is refused\nbefore anything decrypts, with the same uniform NOT_FOUND a missing id gets.\nCUSTODY: the item value is the WHOLE config-values bundle, JSON, encrypted through the same org-bound v2\nenvelope as credentialsCiphertext (data/crypto envelopeEncrypt) - one crypto path, not a second one to audit.\nItems stay OWNER-scoped (decisions.md 2026-07-27): an org-shared config's item belongs to the admin who typed\nit, so a same-org peer is 'unreachable' and keeps the pre-WS-C binding - the residual for the cutover review.\nRULE 10: credentialsCiphertext is still the LIVE read; the Cofre item is the SHADOW, and every credential read\nat the composition-root seam runs compareCredentialShadow (match | drift | shadow_absent | shadow_unreachable |\nshadow_locked | shadow_refused | legacy_absent | shadow_error). The report carries field NAMES only, never a\nvalue. CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE 2026-08-15 (decisions.md), matching the legacy-runtime-tier review date.\nNOT shadowed - live from day one: the credential-egress allow-list is now the ITEM's boundOrigins (empty, i.e.\nREFUSE, once the grant is revoked), not a derivation from the definition an agent authors. Reserved rows\n(platform-oauth / pipedream) are out of WS-C scope and mint nothing.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice B2) - THE INTEGRATION -> COFRE-ITEM JOIN (WS-C shadow).\nintegration_configs gains cofreItemId; cofre_items gains integrationLink {integrationKey, configId}. The join\nis two-way and BOTH halves are stamped server-side: the wire schema CofreItemCreateRequest does not declare\nintegrationLink, so a client cannot forge the provenance. Every read re-checks it - an item id alone is not\nauthority, so a config pointed at another integration's, another config's or another tenant's item is refused\nbefore anything decrypts, with the same uniform NOT_FOUND a missing id gets.\nCUSTODY: the item value is the WHOLE config-values bundle, JSON, encrypted through the same org-bound v2\nenvelope as credentialsCiphertext (data/crypto envelopeEncrypt) - one crypto path, not a second one to audit.\nItems stay OWNER-scoped (decisions.md 2026-07-27): an org-shared config's item belongs to the admin who typed\nit, so a same-org peer is 'unreachable' and keeps the pre-WS-C binding - the residual for the cutover review.\nRULE 10: credentialsCiphertext is still the LIVE read; the Cofre item is the SHADOW, and every credential read\nat the composition-root seam runs compareCredentialShadow (match | drift | shadow_absent | shadow_unreachable |\nshadow_locked | shadow_refused | legacy_absent | shadow_error). The report carries field NAMES only, never a\nvalue. CUTOVER-OR-REMOVE 2026-08-15 (decisions.md), matching the legacy-runtime-tier review date.\nNOT shadowed - live from day one: the credential-egress allow-list is now the ITEM's boundOrigins (empty, i.e.\nREFUSE, once the grant is revoked), not a derivation from the definition an agent authors. Reserved rows\n(platform-oauth / pipedream) are out of WS-C scope and mint nothing.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
