      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice E2) - THE FROZEN PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT.\nintegration_definitions gains TWO fields; no new collection.\n\npublishedSnapshot { scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy, scrubVersion, config, skillMd, lessons?, modelPass\n  {status:'applied'|'skipped'|'failed', reason?, spansApplied?}, redactionCount,\n  supersedes?{scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy} }\n  ONE field = ONE live snapshot. A re-publish REPLACES it wholesale and stamps `supersedes` with\n  the replaced one - that IS the supersede protocol; there is no version chain to choose between.\n  No separate snapshots collection, on A1's reasoning for actions[] being inline: it has no\n  lifecycle apart from its definition, and a second doc is a second thing that can be missing.\n  WRITTEN ONLY by IntegrationDefinitionStore.publishSnapshot, in the SAME gated CAS write that\n  sets visibility:'global' - a published row and its scrubbed artifact cannot disagree.\n  PRESERVED by create(onConflict:'replace'): a content write must not silently return a published\n  row to serving its LIVE bytes cross-org.\n\npublishRequest { requestedBy, requestedAt, note? }\n  The AUTHOR-INITIATED submit-for-review state (closes the E1 review's deferred F2). Presence is\n  the ONLY thing that makes an `org` row visible to a super-admin who is not a member of the org;\n  a `private` row is never submittable. Survives publication so publish/un-publish stay inverse.\n  Review queue = listPublishRequests (super-admin), its own surface, NOT folded into listForActor.\n\nREAD DIRECTION (definition-registry.crossOrgView): a row of ANOTHER org - which the A1 gate means\nis always `global` - is projected from publishedSnapshot; with no snapshot, through the\ndeterministic publish FLOOR at read time. Own-org rows are untouched. This is the single point\nevery reader passes, INCLUDING the credential-egress origin resolver, so a consuming org's\nallow-list is the reviewed artifact's baseUrls and not the author's live ones.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice E2) - THE FROZEN PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT.\nintegration_definitions gains TWO fields; no new collection.\n\npublishedSnapshot { scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy, scrubVersion, config, skillMd, lessons?, modelPass\n  {status:'applied'|'skipped'|'failed', reason?, spansApplied?}, redactionCount,\n  supersedes?{scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy} }\n  ONE field = ONE live snapshot. A re-publish REPLACES it wholesale and stamps `supersedes` with\n  the replaced one - that IS the supersede protocol; there is no version chain to choose between.\n  No separate snapshots collection, on A1's reasoning for actions[] being inline: it has no\n  lifecycle apart from its definition, and a second doc is a second thing that can be missing.\n  WRITTEN ONLY by IntegrationDefinitionStore.publishSnapshot, in the SAME gated CAS write that\n  sets visibility:'global' - a published row and its scrubbed artifact cannot disagree.\n  PRESERVED by create(onConflict:'replace'): a content write must not silently return a published\n  row to serving its LIVE bytes cross-org.\n\npublishRequest { requestedBy, requestedAt, note? }\n  The AUTHOR-INITIATED submit-for-review state (closes the E1 review's deferred F2). Presence is\n  the ONLY thing that makes an `org` row visible to a super-admin who is not a member of the org;\n  a `private` row is never submittable. Survives publication so publish/un-publish stay inverse.\n  Review queue = listPublishRequests (super-admin), its own surface, NOT folded into listForActor.\n\nREAD DIRECTION (definition-registry.crossOrgView): a row of ANOTHER org - which the A1 gate means\nis always `global` - is projected from publishedSnapshot; with no snapshot, through the\ndeterministic publish FLOOR at read time. Own-org rows are untouched. This is the single point\nevery reader passes, INCLUDING the credential-egress origin resolver, so a consuming org's\nallow-list is the reviewed artifact's baseUrls and not the author's live ones.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ]
}